IMPORT prelude

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 5), 2002 Revised Edition:
-- the First Schedule (fees, Parts I to V), the Second Schedule (Radio Amateur Examination fees) and the Third Schedule
-- (conditions of the class licence).  Text: subjects/sg/telecommunications-radio-communication-regulations-2001/registers/source-bundle/TA1999-RG5.txt.
-- A fee function returns the dollar fee, or NOTHING where the table does not say (the type is not in the table, or a bandwidth falls on
-- a boundary that the table's strict inequalities leave out).  Later amendments to these tables are in sgta-i-rg5-amendments.l4.
-- Bandwidths are in kHz (1 MHz = 1000 kHz).

§ `Rg 5 First Schedule Part I: fees for station (spectrum) licence and network (spectrum) licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1284 | PART I
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1285 | FEES FOR STATION (SPECTRUM) LICENCE AND NETWORK
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1286 | (SPECTRUM) LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1288 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1290 | Types of licences Fee payable per annum
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1291 | 1. General Radio-communication Station —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1292 | (a) Base or Fixed Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1293 | (b) Mobile Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1294 | (c) Fixed Link or Relay Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1297 | 2. Wide-area Private Network —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1298 | (a) Portable or Mobile Station $500 per group of 50 stations or part
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1299 | thereof
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1300 | (b) Base or Repeater Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1303 | 3. Public Mobile Network —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1304 | (a) 300 Base Stations or less $100 per station
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1305 | (b) 301 to 500 Base Stations $80 per station for all stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1306 | (c) 501 to 700 Base Stations $60 per station for all stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1307 | (d) 701 Base Stations or more $40 per station for all stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1310 | 4. Fixed Wireless Network $500 per group of 50 stations or part
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1311 | thereof.
@ref Rg 5 First Schedule Part I (src:TA1999-RG5:1284-1311)
GIVEN `type of licence and station` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part I item 1 and item 2(b): the fee payable per annum in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station: Base or Fixed Station" THEN JUST 100
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station: Mobile Station" THEN JUST 50
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station: Fixed Link or Relay Station" THEN JUST 100
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Wide-area Private Network: Base or Repeater Station" THEN JUST 100
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `number of portable or mobile stations (Wide-area Private Network) or stations (Fixed Wireless Network)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part I items 2(a) and 4: the fee per annum in dollars, $500 per group of 50 stations or part thereof` MEANS
    500 TIMES (FLOOR ((`number of portable or mobile stations (Wide-area Private Network) or stations (Fixed Wireless Network)` PLUS 49) DIVIDED BY 50))

GIVEN `number of base stations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part I item 3: the fee per annum in dollars for a Public Mobile Network` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `number of base stations` AT MOST 300 THEN 100 TIMES `number of base stations`
           IF `number of base stations` AT MOST 500 THEN 80 TIMES `number of base stations`
           IF `number of base stations` AT MOST 700 THEN 60 TIMES `number of base stations`
           OTHERWISE 40 TIMES `number of base stations`

§ `Rg 5 First Schedule Part II: fees for station licence and network licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1313 | PART II
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1314 | FEES FOR STATION LICENCE AND NETWORK LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1316 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1318 | Types of licences Fee payable per annum
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1319 | 1. Ship Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1322 | 2. Aircraft Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1325 | 3. Amateur Station —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1326 | (a) General Class $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1327 | (b) Restricted Class $25
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1330 | 4. Experimental Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1333 | 5. Localised Radio-communication Station
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1335 | (a) Remote Control Devices (aircraft models (i) $25 (Personal use)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1336 | and cranes)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1337 | (ii) $50 (Business use)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1340 | (b) Local Area Paging Devices Base Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1343 | (c) Wireless Microphones (i) $25 (Personal use)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1344 | (ii) $50 (Business use)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1347 | (d) Transceivers (CB Walkie Talkies) (i) $25 (Personal use)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1348 | (ii) $50 (Business use)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1351 | (e) Telemetry or Alarm Systems or both $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1352 | (f) Wireless Data or Voice Systems (i) $50 for 50 stations or less
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1353 | (ii) $100 for more than 50 stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1356 | 6. General Radio-communication Station —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1357 | (a) Base or Fixed Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1358 | (b) Mobile Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1359 | (c) Fixed Link or Relay Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1360 | (d) Radiodetermination Station $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1361 | (e) Coast Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1362 | (f) Aeronautical Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1365 | 7. Satellite Communication Station —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1366 | (a) Very Small Aperture Terminal (VSAT) $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1367 | (b) Tracking, Telemetry and Command (TT $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1368 | & C) Earth Station
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1369 | (c) Earth Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1370 | (d) Portable Satellite Communication $50
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1371 | Terminal
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1374 | 8. Localised Private Network —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1375 | (a) Portable or Mobile Station $100 per network
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1376 | (b) Base or Repeater Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1379 | 9. Wide-area Private Network —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1380 | (a) Portable or Mobile Station $500 per group of 50 stations or part
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1381 | thereof
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1382 | (b) Base or Repeater Station $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1385 | 10. Public Mobile Network —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1386 | (a) 300 Base Stations or less $100 per station
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1387 | (b) 301 to 500 Base Stations $80 per station for all stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1388 | (c) 501 to 700 Base Stations $60 per station for all stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1389 | (d) 701 Base Stations or more $40 per station for all stations
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1392 | 11. Fixed Wireless Network $500 per group of 50 stations or part
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1393 | thereof.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1396 | 12. Special Purpose Station $50.
@ref Rg 5 First Schedule Part II (src:TA1999-RG5:1313-1396)
GIVEN `type of licence and station` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part II: the fee payable per annum in dollars, for a type with one fee` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Ship Station" THEN JUST 50
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Aircraft Station" THEN JUST 50
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Amateur Station: General Class" THEN JUST 50
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Amateur Station: Restricted Class" THEN JUST 25
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Experimental Station" THEN JUST 50
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Localised Radio-communication Station: Local Area Paging Devices Base Station" THEN JUST 50
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Localised Radio-communication Station: Telemetry or Alarm Systems or both" THEN JUST 50
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station: Base or Fixed Station" THEN JUST 100
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station: Mobile Station" THEN JUST 50
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station: Fixed Link or Relay Station" THEN JUST 100
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station: Radiodetermination Station" THEN JUST 50
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station: Coast Station" THEN JUST 100
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "General Radio-communication Station: Aeronautical Station" THEN JUST 100
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Satellite Communication Station: Very Small Aperture Terminal (VSAT)" THEN JUST 100
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Satellite Communication Station: Tracking, Telemetry and Command (TT & C) Earth Station" THEN JUST 100
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Satellite Communication Station: Earth Station" THEN JUST 100
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Satellite Communication Station: Portable Satellite Communication Terminal" THEN JUST 50
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Localised Private Network: Base or Repeater Station" THEN JUST 100
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Localised Private Network: Portable or Mobile Station (per network)" THEN JUST 100
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Wide-area Private Network: Base or Repeater Station" THEN JUST 100
           IF `type of licence and station` EQUALS "Special Purpose Station" THEN JUST 50
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `kind of localised radio-communication equipment` IS A STRING
      `business use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part II item 5(a), (c), (d): the fee per annum in dollars, personal use or business use` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (   `kind of localised radio-communication equipment` EQUALS "Remote Control Devices (aircraft models and cranes)"
                   OR `kind of localised radio-communication equipment` EQUALS "Wireless Microphones"
                   OR `kind of localised radio-communication equipment` EQUALS "Transceivers (CB Walkie Talkies)") THEN NOTHING
           IF `business use` THEN JUST 50
           OTHERWISE JUST 25

GIVEN `number of stations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part II item 5(f): the fee per annum in dollars for Wireless Data or Voice Systems` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `number of stations` AT MOST 50 THEN 50
           OTHERWISE 100

GIVEN `number of portable or mobile stations (Wide-area Private Network) or stations (Fixed Wireless Network)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part II items 9(a) and 11: the fee per annum in dollars, $500 per group of 50 stations or part thereof` MEANS
    500 TIMES (FLOOR ((`number of portable or mobile stations (Wide-area Private Network) or stations (Fixed Wireless Network)` PLUS 49) DIVIDED BY 50))

GIVEN `number of base stations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part II item 10: the fee per annum in dollars for a Public Mobile Network` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `number of base stations` AT MOST 300 THEN 100 TIMES `number of base stations`
           IF `number of base stations` AT MOST 500 THEN 80 TIMES `number of base stations`
           IF `number of base stations` AT MOST 700 THEN 60 TIMES `number of base stations`
           OTHERWISE 40 TIMES `number of base stations`

§ `Rg 5 First Schedule Part III: application and processing fees for use of radio frequency`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1398 | PART III
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1399 | APPLICATION AND PROCESSING FEES FOR USE OF RADIO
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1400 | FREQUENCY
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1402 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1404 | Category Fee payable per frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1405 | 1. Commonly Assigned Frequencies $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1406 | (for temporary or occasional use)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1409 | 2. All Other Frequencies —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1410 | (a) bandwidth of 25 kHz or less $290
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1411 | (b) bandwidth of more than 25 kHz but less than $450
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1412 | 500 kHz
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1413 | (c) bandwidth of 500 kHz or more but less than 1 $1,350
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1414 | MHz
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1415 | (d) bandwidth of 1 MHz or more but less than 20 $2,700
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1416 | MHz
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1417 | (e) bandwidth of 20 MHz or more $4,650
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1420 | 3. Satellite Downlink Frequencies $750 per band.
@ref Rg 5 First Schedule Part III (src:TA1999-RG5:1398-1420)
GIVEN `bandwidth in kHz` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part III item 2: the fee per frequency in dollars, all other frequencies` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `bandwidth in kHz` AT MOST 25 THEN 290
           IF `bandwidth in kHz` LESS THAN 500 THEN 450
           IF `bandwidth in kHz` LESS THAN 1000 THEN 1350
           IF `bandwidth in kHz` LESS THAN 20000 THEN 2700
           OTHERWISE 4650

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part III item 1: the fee per frequency in dollars, commonly assigned frequencies (temporary or occasional use)` MEANS 100

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part III item 3: the fee per band in dollars, satellite downlink frequencies` MEANS 750

§ `Rg 5 First Schedule Part IV: annual fees for use of radio frequency`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1422 | PART IV
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1423 | ANNUAL FEES FOR USE OF RADIO FREQUENCY
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1425 | First column Second Column
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1427 | Radio Frequency Spectrum Fee payable per frequency per annum
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1428 | 1. Frequencies for Networks and Systems —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1429 | (a) exclusive use —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1430 | (i) bandwidth of less than 1 MHz $300 per 25 kHz of occupied
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1431 | bandwidth or part thereof
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1432 | (ii) bandwidth of 1 MHz or more $12,000 for the first MHz of occupied
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1433 | bandwidth, and $300 per subsequent
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1434 | MHz of occupied bandwidth or part
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1435 | thereof
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1438 | (b) shared use —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1439 | (i) bandwidth of less than 300 kHz $300 per 25 kHz of occupied
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1440 | bandwidth or part thereof
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1441 | (ii) bandwidth of 300 kHz or more but less $3,500
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1442 | than 20 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1443 | (iii) bandwidth of 20 MHz or more $6,200
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1446 | 2. Satellite Downlink Frequencies $600 per band
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1449 | 3. Common Frequencies for In-building or ISM Band Non ISM Band
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1450 | On-site Wireless Systems —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1451 | (a) bandwidth of 20 MHz or less $50 $100
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1452 | (b) bandwidth of more than 20 MHz but not $100 $200
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1453 | exceeding 50 MHz
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1454 | (c) bandwidth of more than 50 MHz $150 $300
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1457 | 4. Block of Assigned Frequencies for Multi- $15.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1458 | channel Radio-communication Networks and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1459 | Systems
@ref Rg 5 First Schedule Part IV (src:TA1999-RG5:1422-1459)
GIVEN `occupied bandwidth in kHz` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part IV item 1(a): the fee per frequency per annum in dollars, exclusive use` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `occupied bandwidth in kHz` LESS THAN 1000 THEN 300 TIMES (FLOOR ((`occupied bandwidth in kHz` PLUS 24) DIVIDED BY 25))
           OTHERWISE 12000 PLUS (300 TIMES (FLOOR ((`occupied bandwidth in kHz` MINUS 1000 PLUS 999) DIVIDED BY 1000)))

GIVEN `occupied bandwidth in kHz` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part IV item 1(b): the fee per frequency per annum in dollars, shared use` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `occupied bandwidth in kHz` LESS THAN 300 THEN 300 TIMES (FLOOR ((`occupied bandwidth in kHz` PLUS 24) DIVIDED BY 25))
           IF `occupied bandwidth in kHz` LESS THAN 20000 THEN 3500
           OTHERWISE 6200

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part IV item 2: the fee per band per annum in dollars, satellite downlink frequencies` MEANS 600

GIVEN `bandwidth in MHz` IS A NUMBER
      `the frequency is in the ISM Band` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part IV item 3: the fee per annum in dollars, common frequencies for in-building or on-site wireless systems` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `bandwidth in MHz` AT MOST 20 THEN (IF `the frequency is in the ISM Band` THEN 50 ELSE 100)
           IF `bandwidth in MHz` AT MOST 50 THEN (IF `the frequency is in the ISM Band` THEN 100 ELSE 200)
           OTHERWISE (IF `the frequency is in the ISM Band` THEN 150 ELSE 300)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part IV item 4: the fee in dollars, block of assigned frequencies for multi-channel radio-communication networks and systems` MEANS 15

§ `Rg 5 First Schedule Part V: fees for ad hoc temporary radio frequency assignment`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1461 | PART V
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1462 | FEES FOR AD HOC TEMPORARY RADIO FREQUENCY ASSIGNMENT
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1465 | Bandwidth (x) Fee
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1466 | 10 days or less* 11 – 90 days
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1467 | 1. x < 25 kHz $100 $175
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1468 | 2. 25 kHz < x < 500 kHz $150 $275
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1469 | 3. 500 kHz < x < 1 MHz $450 $825
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1470 | 4. 1 MHz < x < 20 MHz $900 $1,625
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1471 | 5. x > 20 MHz $1,550 $2,800.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1472 | * Unless otherwise determined by the Authority, a fee of $100 is payable for the use of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1473 | any of the above radio frequencies if the period of usage or cumulative period of usage is
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1474 | less than 24 hours.
@ref Rg 5 First Schedule Part V (src:TA1999-RG5:1461-1474)
GIVEN `bandwidth in kHz` IS A NUMBER
      `days of use` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part V: the fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `days of use` GREATER THAN 90 THEN NOTHING
           IF `bandwidth in kHz` LESS THAN 25 THEN JUST (IF `days of use` AT MOST 10 THEN 100 ELSE 175)
           IF (`bandwidth in kHz` GREATER THAN 25) AND (`bandwidth in kHz` LESS THAN 500) THEN JUST (IF `days of use` AT MOST 10 THEN 150 ELSE 275)
           IF (`bandwidth in kHz` GREATER THAN 500) AND (`bandwidth in kHz` LESS THAN 1000) THEN JUST (IF `days of use` AT MOST 10 THEN 450 ELSE 825)
           IF (`bandwidth in kHz` GREATER THAN 1000) AND (`bandwidth in kHz` LESS THAN 20000) THEN JUST (IF `days of use` AT MOST 10 THEN 900 ELSE 1625)
           IF `bandwidth in kHz` GREATER THAN 20000 THEN JUST (IF `days of use` AT MOST 10 THEN 1550 ELSE 2800)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Rg 5 Second Schedule: fees for the Radio Amateur Examination`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1475 | SECOND SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1476 | Regulation 39 (2)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1478 | FEES FOR RADIO AMATEUR EXAMINATION
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1480 | First column Second column Third column
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1482 | Type of examination Fee payable by full-time Fee payable by all
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1483 | secondary, pre- other persons
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1484 | university, Institute of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1485 | Technical Education,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1486 | Singapore, and tertiary
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1487 | students
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1488 | 1. Part I (Theory) $20 $40
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1491 | 2. Part II (Morse Sending and $25 $50.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1492 | Receiving)
@ref Rg 5 Second Schedule (src:TA1999-RG5:1475-1492)
GIVEN `the examination is Part I (Theory)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the candidate is a full-time secondary, pre-university, Institute of Technical Education, Singapore, or tertiary student` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 Second Schedule: the fee in dollars to sit the examination` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the examination is Part I (Theory)` THEN (IF `the candidate is a full-time secondary, pre-university, Institute of Technical Education, Singapore, or tertiary student` THEN 20 ELSE 40)
           OTHERWISE (IF `the candidate is a full-time secondary, pre-university, Institute of Technical Education, Singapore, or tertiary student` THEN 25 ELSE 50)

§ `Rg 5 Third Schedule: conditions of the class licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1494 | THIRD SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1495 | Regulation 65 (2) and (4)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1497 | CONDITIONS OF CLASS LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1499 | 1. A class licensee shall comply with the technical specifications laid down from time to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1500 | time by the Authority in relation to the relevant radio-communication station.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1501 | 2. A class licensee shall ensure that the relevant radio-communication station is
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1502 | approved by the Authority before it is used for connection to any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1503 | system or equipment belonging to a public telecommunication licensee, and that the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1504 | relevant radio-communication station is not tampered with or modified in any manner
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1505 | after the approval of the Authority has been obtained.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1506 | 3. A class licensee shall ensure that the relevant radio-communication station is not used
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1507 | for any unlawful purpose.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1508 | 4. The Authority may cancel or suspend a class licence if it is satisfied that the class
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1509 | licensee is contravening, or has contravened and is likely again to contravene, any of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1510 | these conditions or the provisions of the Act.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1512 | [G.N. Nos.S114/2001;S 374/2001; S 450/2001]
@ref Rg 5 Third Schedule (src:TA1999-RG5:1494-1512)
GIVEN `the class licensee complies with the technical specifications the Authority laid down for the relevant radio-communication station` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the station is approved by the Authority before it is used for connection to a public telecommunication licensee's system or equipment, and is not tampered with or modified afterwards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the station is not used for any unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 Third Schedule items 1 to 3: the class licensee is meeting the conditions of the class licence` MEANS
        `the class licensee complies with the technical specifications the Authority laid down for the relevant radio-communication station`
    AND `the station is approved by the Authority before it is used for connection to a public telecommunication licensee's system or equipment, and is not tampered with or modified afterwards`
    AND `the station is not used for any unlawful purpose`

GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied the class licensee is contravening, or has contravened and is likely again to contravene, these conditions or the provisions of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 Third Schedule item 4: the Authority may cancel or suspend the class licence` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied the class licensee is contravening, or has contravened and is likely again to contravene, these conditions or the provisions of the Act`
